WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:08.080
Does India’s oldest political dynasty face
oblivion?

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.809
A defeat in the crucial southern state of
Karnataka suggests that it’s possible.

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:16.490
The Nehru-Gandhi dynasty has stayed close
to, or at the summit of, Indian politics for

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:17.490
nearly 100 years.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:23.670
But for the 47-year-old Gandhi—the son,
grandson, and great-grandson of prime ministers—the

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.920
path to power appears increasingly steep.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.500
Over the past eight years, battered by a series
of electoral defeats, Gandhi has plunged in

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.149
the public imagination from prime minister-in-waiting
to shaky underdog.

00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:40.930
Each defeat amplifies questions about his
inherited privilege, warmed-over policy agenda,

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:43.000
and lack of political skills.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.559
The loss in Karnataka will also hurt Congress’s
ability to raise funds.

00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:51.420
In Prime Minister Narendra Modi and his well-oiled
Bharatiya Janata Party, Mr. Gandhi faces a

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.520
foe both popular and ruthless.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:58.880
As the 2019 general election approaches, Congress
must grapple with arguably its greatest challenge

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.719
since Indian independence seven decades ago.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:07.000
The big question about the party is no longer
“Will it reclaim power?”, but “Will it survive?"

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.780
What do you think about Rahul Gandhi's political future?

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.820
Let us know in your comments. Also, let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:20.660
to cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

